cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite this repository and the relevant scientific references separately."

title: "Atmospheric-Model Sensitivity in Ground-to-Air FSO Receiver Design"

type: software
version: 4.1.0

authors:
  - family-names: "Anika"
    given-names: "Nishat Yasmin"
    affiliation: "Khulna University of Engineering & Technology"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Nishat-Yasmin-Anika/ground-to-air-fso-link-design"

license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-28

abstract: >
  A reproducible computational study investigating ground-to-air
  free-space optical receiver aperture requirements under
  atmospheric attenuation, Gaussian beam collection, pointing
  displacement and weather probability uncertainty.
  The framework incorporates total-variation distributionally
  robust optimization and independent numerical verification.
  The results represent conditional model predictions rather
  than experimentally validated communication performance.

keywords:
  - free-space optical communication
  - ground-to-air optical links
  - atmospheric attenuation
  - Gaussian beam propagation
  - optical receiver aperture
  - pointing errors
  - distributionally robust optimization
  - scientific computing
  - numerical verification
